### Get the current inventory
GET http://localhost:3002/api/v1/inventory

### Delete the current inventory
DELETE http://localhost:3002/api/v1/inventory

### Restock inventory
POST http://localhost:3002/api/v1/inventory/restock

### Submit a simple order
// @name wfrequest
POST http://localhost:3006/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customer": "kendall", "item": "orange", "qty": 3}

### Submit another order
// @name wfrequest_approval
POST http://localhost:3006/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customer": "Veronica", "item": "kiwi", "qty": 2}

### NOTE: `total` is optional. When omitted, the workflow prices the order
### from the inventory catalog as unit price * qty. An explicit `total`
### overrides that — useful e.g. to force the >$1000 approval branch:
POST http://localhost:3006/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customer": "Veronica", "item": "kiwi", "qty": 2, "total": 1299.00}

### Get the status of an order
@instance_id = {{wfrequest.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3006/orders/{{instance_id}}

### Approve an order
@instance_id = {{wfrequest_approval.response.body.instance_id}}

POST http://localhost:3006/orders/{{instance_id}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{"approver": "kendall", "approved": true}

### Sales history for a SKU. Sales are recorded when an order completes, not
### when its stock is reserved, so a failed order leaves no trace here.
GET http://localhost:3002/api/v1/inventory/sales/history?sku=orange

### Deactivate shipping to force the compensation path. An order submitted now
### fails at the shipping step, and the workflow unwinds in reverse: the payment
### is refunded and the reserved stock goes back. Check the inventory before and
### after to see the quantity restored.
###
### Deactivating while an order is in transit breaks the delivery instead: the
### order waits DISPATCH_SECONDS between dispatch and delivery, so submitting an
### order and deactivating during that window fails the delivery workflow. The
### sale is already recorded by then, so the goods are restocked rather than
### released -- the quantity comes back but the sales history keeps the entry.
POST http://localhost:3004/shipping/deactivate

### Reactivate shipping
POST http://localhost:3004/shipping/activate

### Add stock directly (bypasses the agent). Additive, unlike /restock.
POST http://localhost:3002/api/v1/inventory/reposition
Content-Type: application/json

{"items": {"orange": 10, "apple": 5}}

### Ask the agent about stock
// @name agent_stock
POST http://localhost:3005/agent/run
Content-Type: application/json

{"task": "What is the current inventory?"}

### Get the result of the previous run
@instance_id = {{agent_stock.response.body.instance_id}}
GET http://localhost:3005/agent/instances/{{instance_id}}

### Ask the agent for a forecast
POST http://localhost:3005/agent/run
Content-Type: application/json

{"task": "Forecast demand for orange over the next 10 minutes."}

### Ask the agent to restock if needed
POST http://localhost:3005/agent/run
Content-Type: application/json

{"task": "Check every SKU and add stock for anything at risk of running out in the next 10 minutes."}
